{
  "_comment": "Extras for the worksheet /teachers/worksheets/grammar/wechselpraepositionen (Spanish: a or en, going and being), on top of the topic's own exercises: a position/movement rule (the keys keep their old names: regel.wo = position (estar + place word), regel.wohin = movement (a), kasus = the label 'position' / 'movement'; regel.lage = two notes: no stand/lie in Spanish, and poner/meter/colgar/dejar + en), a mascot comic, and picture exercises on the room in src/components/arbeitsblatt/ZimmerSzene.astro (numbers 1–12 are the things in the picture). In segments, a string is text and {\"a\": [...]} is a gap with every accepted answer.",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "regel": {
    "wo": {
      "frage": "¿Dónde está?",
      "kasus": "position",
      "was": "Place: it stays there. Always estar, plus a place word.",
      "verben": [
        "está",
        "están"
      ],
      "beispiel": "El libro <b>está</b> <b>encima de</b> la cama."
    },
    "wohin": {
      "frage": "¿Adónde va?",
      "kasus": "movement",
      "was": "Direction: you go there, or you take it there. Use a.",
      "verben": [
        "ir a",
        "venir a",
        "volver a",
        "llevar a"
      ],
      "beispiel": "<b>Llevo</b> el libro <b>a</b> mi habitación."
    },
    "lage": [
      {
        "form": "no stand / lie",
        "verben": "estar",
        "text": "Spanish does not say whether a thing stands, lies or hangs: it is always estar. La botella y el libro están en la mesa."
      },
      {
        "form": "+ en, not a",
        "verben": "poner · meter · colgar · dejar",
        "text": "The thing moves, but these verbs take en: Pongo el libro en la mesa. Meto la leche en la nevera. Never “a la mesa”."
      }
    ],
    "neun": [
      "en",
      "sobre",
      "encima de",
      "debajo de",
      "delante de",
      "detrás de",
      "al lado de",
      "entre",
      "enfrente de"
    ],
    "kurz": "ir, venir, volver, llevar + a: Voy a la cocina. poner, meter, colgar, dejar + en: Pongo el libro en la mesa. Remember a + el = al and de + el = del: delante del armario, al lado del sofá."
  },
  "comic": {
    "title": "Bruno tidies up",
    "panels": [
      {
        "caption": "poner: where to?",
        "tag": "{poner} + {en} the table (never “a”)",
        "left": {
          "name": "bruno",
          "expr": "happy",
          "say": "{Pongo} el libro {en} la mesa."
        },
        "right": {
          "name": "regi",
          "expr": "thinking",
          "say": "Se mueve, pero con {poner} decimos {en}."
        }
      },
      {
        "caption": "estar: where?",
        "tag": "{está} {en} the table (position)",
        "left": {
          "name": "hamsti",
          "expr": "thinking",
          "say": "¿Y dónde está el libro ahora?"
        },
        "right": {
          "name": "regi",
          "expr": "happy",
          "say": "{Está} {en} la mesa. ¡Se queda ahí!"
        }
      },
      {
        "caption": "ir and llevar: a",
        "tag": "{voy} {a} a place · {llevo} {a} a place",
        "left": {
          "name": "quaki",
          "expr": "happy",
          "say": "{Voy} {a} la cocina."
        },
        "right": {
          "name": "bruno",
          "expr": "celebrate",
          "say": "¡Bien! Yo {llevo} la leche {a} la cocina."
        }
      },
      {
        "caption": "colgar: en",
        "tag": "{cuelgo} + {en} · {está} {en}",
        "left": {
          "name": "hamsti",
          "expr": "happy",
          "say": "{Cuelgo} el cuadro {en} la pared."
        },
        "right": {
          "name": "quaki",
          "expr": "oops",
          "say": "{Está} {en} la pared… ¡pero torcido!"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
